// ML-012a: first real musl static-link E2E milestone. A real
// `int main(void) { return 42; }` (Inputs/musl_e2e_exit.c, no headers, no
// libc calls beyond the implicit startup path) compiled with
// `clang --target=dadao`, then linked -- via the manual llvm-mc-family
// pipeline this project's lit suite already uses for real compiler output
// (same style as clang_hello.test/malloc_hello.test: feed the pieces
// directly to ld.lld rather than going through the full clang driver
// link) -- against musl's REAL crt1.o and the subset of libc.a that
// currently compiles clean (.work/build/musl/lib/{crt1.o,libc.a}, built
// from arch/dadao/{crt_arch.h,arch.mak} + src/env/dadao/
// {__libc_start_main.c,__init_tls.c} + the already-landed ML-007a..011a
// arch files). This exercises the real crt1.c -> _start_c ->
// __libc_start_main -> __init_libc/__init_tls/__init_tp ->
// libc_start_main_stage2 -> exit() -> _Exit() -> SYS_exit_group syscall
// path end to end on both backends -- not a hand-assembled probe.
//
// Object-file scope actually linked (see this task's completion notes for
// the full picture): crt1.o (this task, arch/dadao/crt_arch.h) + a
// manually-archived libc.a built from the 1166 (of 1346 candidate)
// src/*.c/.s files that currently compile clean under
// `clang --target=dadao` -- musl's own static-link model only pulls in
// .o's whose symbols are actually referenced, so the ~180 files that still
// fail to compile (all in already-tracked docs/issues.yaml backend-gap
// categories: libcall lowering, dynamic_stackalloc, sign_extend_inreg,
// three internal SelectionDAG assertions, un-analyzable-fallthrough, one
// AsmPrinter UNREACHABLE, one remaining inline-asm-operand-allocation
// case) are simply absent from the archive and never referenced by this
// minimal program's startup path, so their absence causes no link error.
//
// Two real, previously-latent backend/ABI gaps were found and routed
// around (musl-side only, no LLVM/QEMU/gem5 source touched) to reach this
// milestone -- both documented in detail at the point of the fix and in
// docs/issues.yaml:
//   1. DADAOCallingConv.td ("GPRD only, Phase 5 spike") actually passes
//      pointer arguments in the RD bank (rd16), not the RB bank (rb16)
//      contracts/abi/spec.md SS2.1 documents -- crt_arch.h's `call
//      _start_c` and src/thread/dadao/__set_thread_area.s (ML-011a) were
//      both corrected to place/read the pointer argument in rd16 to match
//      the real compiled callee/caller. tp_probe.test was updated to match.
//   2. musl's generic __libc_start_main.c/__init_tls.c hit two independent
//      already-tracked DADAO codegen gaps (codegen-tailcall-lowercall-
//      assert; musl-inline-asm-empty-clobber-reg-alloc) plus one newly
//      found link-time-only gap (a PC-relative relocation used for
//      "address of a weak-undefined external symbol" has no wide-range/
//      absolute fallback, so referencing `_DYNAMIC` -- always weak-
//      undefined-resolves-to-0 in this static-only, no-dynamic-linker
//      project, ADR-0014 D5 -- from code loaded at 0x80000000 overflows
//      the relocation's range). Routed around with arch/dadao/arch.mak
//      (-fno-optimize-sibling-calls, safe/portable, disables an
//      optimization only) and two minimal, single-line-diff arch
//      overrides (src/env/dadao/__libc_start_main.c,
//      src/env/dadao/__init_tls.c) -- see those files' header comments
//      for the full diagnosis. Neither LLVM, QEMU, nor gem5 source was
//      modified.
//
// Exit 42 = int main(void) { return 42; } really executed via the real
// musl startup chain and its return value really propagated through
// exit()/_Exit()/SYS_exit_group all the way to process exit code, on
// BOTH backends.
// RUN: %clang --target=dadao -std=c99 -nostdinc -ffreestanding -O0 \
// RUN:   -c -o %t.o %S/Inputs/musl_e2e_exit.c
// RUN: %ld.lld -T %S/../../scripts/dadao.ld \
// RUN:   --start-group %S/../../../.work/build/musl/lib/crt1.o %t.o %S/../../../.work/build/musl/lib/libc.a --end-group \
// RUN:   -o %t.elf
// RUN: %llvm-objcopy -O binary %t.elf %t.bin
// RUN: bash -c '%qemu -M dadao-m1 -nographic -bios %trampoline -kernel %t.bin > %t.out 2>&1; test $? -eq 42'
// RUN: bash -c '%gem5 %gem5_se %t.elf > %t.gout 2>&1; test $? -eq 42'
